From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:01:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 82/83] runner: no drawn word character glued to an owned span
 that ends in one (the inline mark)

With TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=1 an owned inline value ends in " @engine", and arm() only armed spans ending in a digit,
so nothing guarded the model's first draw after the mark. On Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP1 the model wrote "@engineer" in 4 of
9 replies of the digit-run set; in 13^150 seed 13 it went on to "@engineer-mike/secret-repo!" and a 1,024-digit run
that shares no digit with the value (the gate's one runaway on d306dc2fe and ab34d28c8 alike).

arm() now also arms a span whose tail ends in a word character (TF_RUNNER_MARK_STOP, on by default): the model's
first draw after it may not start with a letter, digit, "_", "-" or "/", and is replaced by the newline as the digit
stop does. The span is the runner's parsed, forced one (its own token count and text), never the model's text. A
space, newline or punctuation after it lands as drawn. A mark stop does not arm the hold, so the model's later
numbers, a full copy of the value included, run to TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_RUN_MAX as before.

Tests: two recorded TP1 replies as fixtures (the failing seed-13 one: base first stops at the 1,025th digit, the
mark stop at "er" of "@engineer"; a passing seed-12 one with a model-written copy of the value: untouched either
way), the rule with its controls (space, "?", newline and ")" land; after_mark off is base), no hold after a mark
stop against a digit stop's hold, the session path with the mark on and off, and the knob.
